  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\vec{a}=\\hat{i}+\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}, \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=1$ and $\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b}=\\vec{j}-\\vec{k}$,<br />Let $\\bar{b}=b_1 \\hat{i}+b_2 \\hat{j}+b_3 \\widehat{k}$<br />Now, $\\hat{j}-\\widehat{k}=\\bar{a} \\times \\bar{b}=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\widehat{k} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ b_2 & b_2 & b_3\\end{array}\\right|$<br />$\\Rightarrow b_3-b_2=0, b_1-b_3=1, b_2-b_1=-1$<br />$\\Rightarrow b_3=b_2, b_1=b_2+1$<br />Also, $\\bar{a} \\cdot \\bar{b}=1$<br />$\\Rightarrow b_1+b_2+b_3=1$<br />$\\Rightarrow 3 b_2+1=1$<br />$\\Rightarrow b_2=0$<br />$\\Rightarrow b_1=1, b_3=0$<br />Thus, $\\bar{b}=\\hat{i}$",
    "image": null
  },
